    '  <h1>Pelican Engine</h1>\n' +
    '  <p><strong>Build games for the web with TypeScript.</strong></p>\n' +
    '  <p>Code-first · WebGPU-first · Designed for human and external AI workflows</p>\n' +
    '  <p>\n' +
    '    <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/pelican-engine"><img src="https://img.shields.io/npm/v/pelican-engine?label=npm&amp;color=168b80" alt="npm version"></a>\n' +
    '    <img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-24536b" alt="MIT license">\n' +
    '    <img src="https://img.shields.io/badge/TypeScript-SDK-3178c6" alt="TypeScript SDK">\n' +
    '  </p>\n' +
    '</div>\n' +
    '\n' +
    'Pelican Engine provides a TypeScript SDK, compiler, runtime, renderer and CLI in one package. Define game content and behavior in code, run a local development server and build a static web distribution. AI tools may assist development, but the game runtime does not include an LLM or AI agent.\n' +
    '\n' +
    '> **Development status:** this is an evolving engine, not a complete first release. Current source behavior, hardware compatibility, performance and the full feature set have not been fully validated. A normal version number is not an acceptance claim. See the [development status](https://github.com/danchar12138/pelican-engine/blob/main/docs/STATUS.md) for known gaps.\n' +
    '\n' +
    '## Quick start\n' +
    '\n' +
    'Install Node.js **24.x** and npm, then create a new empty game directory:\n' +
    '\n' +
    '```sh\n' +
    'mkdir my-pelican-game\n' +
    'cd my-pelican-game\n' +
    'npm --prefix . install --save-dev --save-exact pelican-engine\n' +
    'npx pelican dev\n' +
    '```\n' +
    '\n' +
    'The first `dev` creates `game.ts`, `pelican.project.json` and `AGENTS.md` in an eligible empty project. Existing game files and author instructions are not overwritten. The explicit `--prefix .` prevents npm from choosing a parent project; `--save-exact` pins the installed version. Stop the development server before building:\n' +
    '\n' +
    '```sh\n' +
    'npx --no-install pelican build\n' +
    '```\n' +
    '\n' +
    'Deploy the resulting `dist/` directory, including its generated assets and notices, to an HTTP(S) static host. For a nested deployment, use `npx --no-install pelican build --base /game/`.\n' +
    '\n' +
    'Builds are prepared in a fresh `.pelican/dist-stage-*` directory before the\n' +
    'final `dist` switch. When an existing `dist` is present, it is retained under\n' +
    '`.pelican/dist-backup-*/dist`; the build report includes `previousOutput`.\n' +
    'Failed staging files and backups are not automatically deleted. Inspect and\n' +
    "retain or remove them according to the game owner's needs, without following\n" +
    'links. Stop other processes that modify `dist` during a build: concurrent-change\n' +
    'checks and rollback are best effort, not a cross-process transaction. This new\n' +
    'path and failure recovery have not been runtime-validated.\n' +
    '\n' +
    'Commands use common Node/npm syntax rather than a particular shell. **Engine and game development currently support Windows only**; Linux and macOS development workflows have not been promised or validated. Player platforms are not restricted by brand or OS: actual rendering availability depends on browser and graphics capabilities.\n' +
    '\n' +
    '## Your game\n' +
    '\n' +
    'The generated starter defines a scene and a rotating box. Game code imports only the public package, for example:\n' +
    '\n' +
    '```ts\n' +
    'import { defineGame, defineMaterial, defineScene } from "pelican-engine";\n' +
    '\n' +
    'const material = defineMaterial({ id: "paint", color: "#38b8a4", roughness: 0.45 });\n' +
    'const scene = defineScene({\n' +
    '  id: "main",\n' +
    '  camera: { position: [4, 3, 6], target: [0, 0, 0], fov: 50 },\n' +
    '  entities: [\n' +
    '    { id: "box", mesh: { geometry: { kind: "box" }, material } },\n' +
    '    { id: "light", light: { kind: "directional", intensity: 4 },\n' +
    '      transform: { position: [3, 6, 4] } },\n' +
    '  ],\n' +
    '});\n' +
    'export default defineGame({ id: "my-game", scene });\n' +
    '```\n' +
    '\n' +
    'Save it as `game.ts` in a project created by the CLI. The exact engine version is recorded in `pelican.project.json`. `pelican migrate` can plan an explicit lock update and, with `--apply --from`, create a recovery backup before changing it; see GAME-AUTHOR for the restore protocol. This lock-only command does not migrate game code, dependencies or saves and has not been runtime-validated. Do not edit `node_modules` or import engine internals.\n' +
    '\n' +
    'Useful commands:\n' +
    '\n' +
    '```sh\n' +
    'npx --no-install pelican help\n' +
    'npx --no-install pelican api\n' +
    'npx --no-install pelican api --symbol defineGame\n' +
    'npx --no-install pelican migrate\n' +
    'npx --no-install pelican dev --port 4173\n' +
